// RFC 8985's TLP_send_probe and Linux send no second probe while the first's verdict is open, so the second segment
// would wait for the RTO; Aloe sends one once the first probe's end is acknowledged.
// That is Aloe's one departure from RFC 8985 by the author's decision (7.3 and 7.4.2; Linux's tcp_send_loss_probe).
// The handshake's ACK 10 ms after the SYN-ACK gives an srtt of 10 ms. The first order, written at 10 ms, is lost and
// probed at 10 + 2 * 10 + 40 = 70 ms; the probe arrives, and the ACK at 80 ms lands on its end and echoes it: a sample
// of 10 ms, srtt still 10 ms, and the verdict open, since that ACK may answer either copy. The second order, written at
// 80 ms into the empty queue, is lost too; nothing is in flight but it, so it is probed at 80 + 2 * 10 + 40 = 140 ms,
// and that expiry first closes the first verdict as a loss: NewReno's target max(100 / 2, 2 * 1448) = 2896, the flight
// being the second order, and the window cut to it, as the RFC would cut it at the next ACK past the first probe's
// end. The second probe's ACK at 150 ms lands on its own end, and a write then takes the 2896 the first cut left. Under
// the RFC the second order would have waited for its RTO, 80 + 210 = 290 ms. The TCP page's note on departures lists
// the brick's others.
--congestion=newreno
0 socket(..., SOCK_STREAM, IPPROTO_TCP) = 3
+0 bind(3, ..., ...) = 0
+0 listen(3, 1) = 0

+0 < S 0:0(0) win 65535 <mss 1460,sackOK,TS val 100 ecr 0,nop,wscale 7>
+0 > S. 0:0(0) ack 1 win 65535 <mss 1460,sackOK,TS val 0 ecr 100,nop,wscale 3>
+0.010 < . 1:1(0) ack 1 win 512 <nop,nop,TS val 110 ecr 0>
+0 accept(3, ..., ...) = 4

+0 write(4, ..., 100) = 100
+0 > P. 1:101(100) ack 1 win 46336 <nop,nop,TS val 10 ecr 110>
+0.060 > P. 1:101(100) ack 1 win 46336 <nop,nop,TS val 70 ecr 110>
+0.010 < . 1:1(0) ack 101 win 512 <nop,nop,TS val 180 ecr 70>
+0 write(4, ..., 100) = 100
+0 > P. 101:201(100) ack 1 win 46336 <nop,nop,TS val 80 ecr 180>
+0.060 > P. 101:201(100) ack 1 win 46336 <nop,nop,TS val 140 ecr 180>
+0.010 < . 1:1(0) ack 201 win 512 <nop,nop,TS val 250 ecr 140>
+0 write(4, ..., 20000) = 2896
+0 > P. 201:1649(1448) ack 1 win 46336 <nop,nop,TS val 150 ecr 250>
+0 > P. 1649:3097(1448) ack 1 win 46336 <nop,nop,TS val 150 ecr 250>
+0.010 < . 1:1(0) ack 3097 win 512 <nop,nop,TS val 260 ecr 150>
